    "updated_at": "2017-03-19T03:42:44Z",
    "body": "Yikes, I hadn't thought about this:\r\n\r\n> This means that when our more active users that participate on multiple wikis (Wikimedia hosts over 800 wikis, including 284 active Wikipedia subdomains), you visit a wiki, even once, that module cache is populated, but until you visit that wiki again, we have no way to clear it. The modules may have changed many times since then, and would be pruned immediately when viewed, but still it's taking up precious space and preventing other wikis from claiming space instead (in Firefox). ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
