    "updated_at": "2024-01-13T11:05:30Z",
    "body": "Not entirely sure if this is the right place to chime in, but just in case: We use indexeddb to buffer map data for a browser game. The game is organized in rounds on different subdomains, each of which will shut down at some point, when players will no longer visit the map and buffered data will needlessly persist. We're talking up to a couple of hundred MB each.\r\n\r\nAs such, +1.",
