    "created_at": "2024-05-06T05:20:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-05-06T05:20:08Z",
    "body": "Likewise, I am using indexeddb as a buffer cache for a context that might be visited again but likely won't be (I cannot use a service worker in this case) and will be hundreds of megabytes, potentially gigabytes.\r\n\r\nCurrently the browser will persist the data indefinitely however it would be ideal if I could set an expiry on a key so it could remove itself if it has not been accessed within that time.",
